{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cftm1DWm7o2c4KsaCqSvK","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I blessed nine of the ten amended rows and sent SR-046 back again. LLR-326 and TC-350 are approved. All three commits passed the pre-commit checks.\n\n**Verdict** (`f33eaf48`, trailer `WI: WI-880`, file `docs/reviews/wi-880/002-ADJUDICATE-2296cce.md`)\n\n**Amendment: `VERDICT: MEANING rows=10`.** Every row adds an obligation.\n- **Blessed (9):** SR-019, SR-020, SR-032, LLR-021, LLR-047, LLR-322, TC-021, TC-047, TC-345.\n  - **SR-032:** its Windows install clause now names this repository's own setup (D-002), and `scripts/dev-setup.ps1` matches it. One observation, not a return: the Requirement cell still speaks only of the shipped templates.\n  - **LLR-322:** it now states the three this-repo obligations that TC-345 checks, so TC-345 has a home for each of them.\n  - **LLR-047:** its narrowed claim is true of the code. Bare `python` is exact on every platform, and `python3` only on POSIX. The reason for not shimming `python3` on Windows (D-003) holds up: a `.cmd` shim re-parses its arguments and reopens the WI-227 argument contract.\n- **Not blessed: SR-046.** Its new wording, \"a bare runtime name its platform provides\", doesn't close on Windows. The official Python install manager provides `python3` there, and I reproduced the failure on this box: with the menu on 3.11, a `[run]` line using `python3` ran `Python312\\python.exe`. A natural reading therefore requires `python3` to be exact on Windows, which LLR-047 deliberately doesn't deliver. The fix is to state the split LLR-047 already decides: `python` everywhere, `python3` on POSIX.\n\n**First approval: `OUTCOME: APPROVE rows=2`.** SR-032's blessed clause now calls for LLR-326, and the code matches it. LLR-326 and TC-350 now agree that the runtime search runs again after either answer.\n\n**Acts:**\n- **Re-attestation** (`971ff71d`, act 93): LLR-021, LLR-047, LLR-322, TC-021, TC-047 and TC-345 are re-anchored.\n- **Approval** (`388d1175`): LLR-326 and TC-350 moved from `Drafted` to `Approved`, with the snapshot of their two registries in the same commit. Only those two Status cells changed.\n\n**Still open:** SR-019, SR-020 and SR-032 are blessed but not re-anchored. SR-046's drift is in the same registry, and the copy refuses while it drifts, so I didn't attempt it. Put them in the same sitting as the corrected SR-046.\n\n**Decision for you:** the SR-046 follow-up draft sits under the amendment heading in the verdict file. Intake won't mint it from WI-880's ordinary spec, so it needs routing back to the lane.\n\n**Tests:** the arms-map tests plus the run-menu suite ran 32 passed, 2 skipped. Both skips are because this box is Windows: one test needs a pseudo-terminal, the other is POSIX-only."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":767,"cache_read_input_tokens":231115,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":767},"output_tokens":843,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7a511e73-e906-4589-9f31-ae73f8534ed7","uuid":"96b153e2-be13-4742-b000-c9ef261eca0c","timestamp":"2026-10-10T15:02:55.711Z","request_id":"req_011Cftm1D2EwcmNecfyUgDDY"}
